  "interpretation": [
    "All 30 batch application-ready records completed below one second in this run. Window preparation was skipped on the warm batch; show+barrier includes Wails ShowWindow and its queued ScreenGetAll barrier, so the components cannot be separated from these timings.",
    "Main private memory and GPU private memory fell from their batch peaks after hiding. Renderer private memory remained substantially above its pre-batch level through 180 seconds; the tree did not return to its original platform.",
    "GDI and handle plateaus are reported independently from private-memory retention. These observations do not prove the absence of a leak or establish that retained renderer memory is an unbounded leak.",
    "Read-only frontend review found cleanup for prior image loads, Image.src, canvas backing sizes, listener/abort handlers, editor timers and observers; no definite stale-frame reference was identified. Browser allocator/cache retention was not measured with a heap profiler."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The first diagnostic screenshot occurred before the sampler started, so this run has no hidden cold-process memory baseline. The pre-batch comparison is an already-initialized runtime.",
    "An initial Codex prewarm child plus conhost expired after five minutes; their approximately 32 MiB private-memory drop is not attributed to screenshot cleanup. Per-process details remain in raw samples.",
    "Concurrent automation, tool execution and harness compilation affected host load. Results describe this observed cohort rather than an isolated benchmark or a universal latency guarantee.",
    "The configured 2-second cadence can have jitter and catch-up samples. Actual UTC timestamps are retained, and platform medians are unweighted sample medians.",
    "Working-set sums may double-count shared pages. Private-memory values include allocator retention; no forced GC, working-set trimming, UI operations or API/model requests were issued by the sampler.",
    "Windows Graphics Capture timed out and coordinate geometry was unavailable to the automation engine, so visual screenshot/editor/overlay quality was not evaluated.",
    "Immediate window lists can lag and text-only UIA can expose hidden trees or later calls can reactivate a window. The earlier Escape failure interpretation is inconclusive; this run confirmed hiding by refreshing the list while the process remained alive.",
    "No focus patch was applied. Ordinary screenshot measurements do not validate scrolling alignment or the independent later scroll fix."
  ],
